---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Get Help" description="Find a next step for urgent help, local support, or talking with a mental health professional.">
  <div class="container narrow section">
    <header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">You can reach out</p><h1>Support for right now.</h1><p>You do not need to find the perfect words to ask for help.</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="callout"><h2>If there is immediate danger</h2><p>If you or someone else is in immediate danger, contact your local emergency services or go to the nearest emergency department. If you can do so safely, ask someone you trust to stay with you while you get support.</p></div>
      <h2>Find a helpline near you</h2>
      <p><a href="https://findahelpline.com/" rel="external noreferrer">Find A Helpline</a> is a third-party directory that lets you look for phone, text, and chat services by country and topic.</p>
      <p><a class="button" href="https://findahelpline.com/" rel="external noreferrer">Find local support <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
      <p>Check the service's current hours, location coverage, cost, and privacy information before using it. Availability and the support offered vary. We do not operate this directory or independently verify each listing.</p>
      <h2>If you are looking for ongoing support</h2>
      <p>A primary care professional or a local mental health service can explain options in your area. You can ask about the cost, waiting time, language support, and what happens at a first appointment.</p>
      <p>If reaching out feels difficult, you could write a short note first: “I have been finding things hard, and I would like to talk about support.” A trusted person may be able to help you make the call or attend an appointment.</p>
      <h2>If you are supporting someone else</h2>
      <p>You can listen, ask what would help, and offer to look for local support together. If there is immediate danger, contact local emergency services. You do not have to manage an urgent situation alone.</p>
      <h2>About this page</h2>
      <p>Psychology Blog is an educational website. It has no monitored support inbox, crisis response team, or live chat. Do not send urgent requests or private health details through the site.</p>
      <p>Country-specific crisis numbers have not been added because they need human verification. Use the external directory or your local services for current contact details.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
